From e198050f64bbcbc4d13b2c3abcccd2ce80c63016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:12:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] caas: Raise PRODUCT_SHIPPING_API_LEVEL to 37 for Android 17

With the 6.18.38 kernel there is no ashmem (CONFIG_ASHMEM now needs
Rust) and no ashmem ioctl compatibility on memfds, and the device
runs with sys.use_memfd=true.

At PRODUCT_SHIPPING_API_LEVEL 35, ro.vendor.api_level is 202404.
Chromium/WebView then creates and seals shared memory through
libandroid ASharedMemory_*, which ends in libcutils. libcutils
detects memfds with readlink(/proc/self/fd/N), which the Chromium
renderer seccomp policy denies with EPERM. libcutils then falls
back to the ashmem ioctls, which fail without kernel ashmem. The
renderer spins on "Unable to stat ashmem device" and no web content
renders in the browser (video or otherwise).

Shipping level 37 makes ro.vendor.api_level 202604 (Android 17).
Chromium then uses its own memfd_create/F_ADD_SEALS path and no
longer goes through libcutils. sys.use_memfd=true is still needed
so that apps targeting SDK < 37 get memfds.

Also raise the BASE_LTS2024_ANDROID_KERNEL shipping level from 34
to 35.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1704
Signed-off-by: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
---
 groups/device-specific/caas/caas.mk | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/groups/device-specific/caas/caas.mk b/groups/device-specific/caas/caas.mk
index 9950d73e..ff72579d 100644
--- a/groups/device-specific/caas/caas.mk
+++ b/groups/device-specific/caas/caas.mk
@@ -83,10 +83,10 @@ PRODUCT_SET_DEBUGFS_RESTRICTIONS := true
 endif
 {{^ota-update}}
 ifeq ($(BASE_LTS2024_ANDROID_KERNEL), true)
-PRODUCT_SHIPPING_API_LEVEL := 34
+PRODUCT_SHIPPING_API_LEVEL := 35
 PRODUCT_OTA_ENFORCE_VINTF_KERNEL_REQUIREMENTS := false
 else
-PRODUCT_SHIPPING_API_LEVEL := 35
+PRODUCT_SHIPPING_API_LEVEL := 37
 PRODUCT_OTA_ENFORCE_VINTF_KERNEL_REQUIREMENTS := true
 endif
 {{/ota-update}}
-- 
2.34.1

